-- title:
--   Separation of good points centring a place (q=2)
-- statement:
--   The setting is the Igusa leg of the semistable covering data for a prime $q$ which is assumed equal to $2$, and a level $M'$ (nonzero) with $q \nmid M'$. Fixed are: a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; a finite set $W$ of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A, M')$ over the residue field of $A$, where `modularFunctionFieldC K M'` is the subfield of $K$-Laurent series generated by the $q$-expansions `jqModC K` and `jqNModC K M'`, and `hW` says that $W$ consists exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, that is of the rational places $w$ satisfying the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace` for which $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen})$ lies in `ssJSet q`, the set of those $j$ such that every elliptic curve with invariant $j$ over the field in question has no nonzero $q$-torsion point; and an inclusion `hle` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` (the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change, inside Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, of the full level-$M'$ modular function field) into `fieldBar q M'` $=$ `xHFunctionFieldBar (q^2 * M') (levelH q M')`, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the function field of the $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ with $H =$ `levelH q M'` the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$.
--
--   The hypotheses fall into the following groups, all of which are assumptions of the theorem.
--
--   Reduction data: a `ConstantReduction` $R_0$ of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` (a valuation subring `R₀.integers`, a surjective residue homomorphism with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places, and the compatibility axioms of that structure), together with `hR₀`: for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element belongs to `R₀.integers` and its residue, read as a Laurent series over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   Igusa charts: a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ (an element of `Idx q`) and a family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'` indexed by the projective line $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$, subject to: `hIg_inf`, which describes $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ at the point `lineInfty q` as the Gauss ring, namely $f$ belongs to it precisely when $f = x/y$ for Laurent series $x,y$ with coefficients in $A$ such that the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ is nonzero; `hIg`, that every $\ell \in \mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ is $\mathrm{redQ}\,\gamma$-translated from $\infty$ for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the pullback of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj`, injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$; and `hIg_perm`, that for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ the pullbacks along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permute the family.
--
--   Supersingular charts: a family $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ of valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'` indexed by $W$, subject to: `hSS_A`, that an element of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ exactly when it lies in $A$; `hSS_over`, that for $s \in W$ and $f \in$ `R₀.integers` which has no pole at any place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ where the base-changed $q$-expansion of $j$ has none, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and, for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference of that image and $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$; `hSS_fix`, invariance of each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ under pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; and `hSS_tr`, the existence for each $s$ of $t \in O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ with $t - a$ a unit of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ for every $a \in A$.
--
--   Prolongation data: a `RegularProlongation` $R$ of $A$ from `fieldBar q M'` to `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2 * M') (levelH q M')` with `hR` identifying `R.integers` with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$, and `hR₀O` saying that $f$ lies in `R₀.integers` precisely when its image in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$.
--
--   Uniformiser data: an element $\pi \in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$.
--
--   Small-field data: an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0 \cap A$ such that $A \cap k_0$ is a henselian discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ and algebraically closed residue field, together with `hκ`: every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0 \cap A$.
--
--   Auxiliary prime data: a prime $\ell \ge 3$ with $\ell \neq q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$, an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity, and $\varpi_t \in k_0 \cap A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   Finite layer: an intermediate field $K_1$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$, finite over $k_0$, and a valuation subring $A_1$ of $K_1$ consisting of the elements of $K_1$ lying in $A$, assumed to be a henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   The field `fieldBar q M'` carries the $k_0$-algebra structure obtained from $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`. The assertion is then universally quantified over the following further data. First, an intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ such that: the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is all of `fieldBar q M'`; $F_0$ is stable under every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every $K'$-linearly independent family $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and every family $a$ of elements of the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces $a_i = 0$ for all $i$; and every element of `fieldBar q M'` whose underlying Laurent series lies in the image of `coeffEmb` (that is, has rational coefficients) belongs to $F_0$. Write $T_1$ for the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield of `fieldBar q M'` generated by the image of $K_1$. Second, an $A_1$-algebra structure on $T_1$ whose structure map agrees with $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'` on $A_1 \subseteq K_1 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$. Third, an element $j_1 \in T_1$ whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is the image under `hle` of the base-changed $q$-expansion `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq` of the modular invariant, and which is nonzero.
--
--   The scheme in play is $\mathfrak X_1 =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ T₁ j₁`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout glueing $X_{\mathrm{Fin}} = \operatorname{Spec}$ of the integral closure of $A_1[j_1]$ in $T_1$ to $X_{\infty} = \operatorname{Spec}$ of the integral closure of $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$ in $T_1$, with canonical morphisms `ιFin`, `ιInf` and structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$. Three auxiliary predicates are introduced. For $x \in \mathfrak X_1$ and $f \in T_1$, `InStalk x f` holds when, for every point $y$ of either chart mapping to $x$, there are chart elements $g,h$ with $h \notin y$ and $fh = g$ in $T_1$; `InMax x f` is the same with the additional requirement $g \in y$. For a place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, `Centred P x` holds when $P$ is rational (the structure map $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to P$'s residue field is surjective) and every $f$ with `InStalk x f` lies in the valuation subring of $P$, has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and satisfies: the $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ is $< 1$ if and only if `InMax x f`. Finally, `GoodPt x` is the conjunction of: `toBase` maps $x$ to the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$; $x$ specialises only to itself; for every point $y$ of either chart over $x$, every chart element whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is a non-unit of `R.integers` lies in $y$; and, for every point $y$ of the finite chart over $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the finite chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(\mathtt{jChartFin})$ does not lie in `ssJSet q Ω`.
--
--   The conclusion is the separation statement: for all points $x, x'$ of $\mathfrak X_1$ satisfying `GoodPt` and every place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, if `Centred P x` and `Centred P x'` both hold then $x = x'$.
--
--   This is the uniqueness (separation) clause for centres of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-rational places on the two-chart integral model of the full-level field: the formal discs around distinct good points of the special fibre are disjoint. It is the $q = 2$ case, parallel to the version assuming $5 \le q$, and it is used in the construction of the smooth Igusa base model, [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaBaseModel_smoothPointStalks_of_eq_two`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaBaseModel_smoothPointStalks_of_eq_two).
